// T5 - the stored XSure instance loads against the rewritten MetaModel and still holds its data.
//
// XSure is one of the two FML-RT fixtures migrated out of MULTIProcessChallenge.prj. Migrating it
// was not a base-URI rewrite: the rewritten MetaModel NESTS TaskType inside ProcessType, so
// "#TaskType" became "#ProcessType#TaskType" in every flexoConceptURI. The legacy file also stored
// roleName="in" while its own metamodel declared the role as "_in" - a dangling reference since day
// one, repaired on the way.
//
// It asserts business values, not merely that the file parses: an insurance claim-handling process
// with its actors, actor types and artifact types.

xsure = load -r ["http://openflexo.org/multi-process-challenge/XSure.fml.rt"];
assert xsure != null;

// The process definition itself.
assert xsure.allProcessTypes().size == 1;
claimHandling = xsure.getProcessType("Claim Handling");
assert claimHandling != null;
assert claimHandling.name == "Claim Handling";

// Who may act: three actors, five roles they can hold.
assert xsure.allActors().size == 3;
assert xsure.getActor("Ben Boss") != null;
assert xsure.getActor("John Smith") != null;
assert xsure.getActor("Paul Alter") != null;

assert xsure.allActorTypes().size == 5;
assert xsure.getActorType("Claim handling manager") != null;
assert xsure.getActorType("Financial officer") != null;
assert xsure.getActorType("Senior Manager") != null;

// What the process handles.
assert xsure.allArtifactTypes().size == 2;
assert xsure.getArtifactType("Claim") != null;
assert xsure.getArtifactType("Claim payment decision") != null;

log "Test PASSED: T5 - the stored XSure instance loads and keeps its business data";
